# Copy to .env.local and fill in. The console reads this at startup, so
# running it is `npm run dev` and nothing else.
#
# .env.local is git-ignored. A real environment variable still wins over
# anything here, so a container or service manager keeps control.
#
# Nothing in this file reaches the browser. The dev server is the proxy: it
# mints the token, adds it to each request on the way through, and serves the
# page only the party map and the seat.

# Which infra/<network>/ directory to read: localnet, devnet, bitsafe.
INDIVISA_NETWORK=localnet

# Which seat to show, matching infra/<network>/demo/seat-<tag>.json.
INDIVISA_TAG=demo

# The service account's secret, for a network whose ui.json carries an `auth`
# block (DevNet). Two identities, and it is worth keeping them apart: this one
# is the PAYING AGENT, a ledger party, and it is what signs the settlement.
# The person at the keyboard is the OPERATOR, who signs in through the browser
# against the `operator` block in ui.json; nothing in this file concerns them.
# LocalNet and the judges' stack are unauthenticated and need neither.
#
# It may also live in infra/<network>/ui.json as auth.clientSecret. Keep it in
# whichever of the two your deployment already protects; do not put it in both.
# INDIVISA_CLIENT_SECRET=
